------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ILE is designed to run alongside the following independent open-source
projects, each distributed under its own license. ILE does not modify or
redistribute them; they are pulled as container images or dependencies at
deploy time:

  - PostgreSQL              (PostgreSQL License)
  - Metabase                (AGPL-3.0 / Enterprise) — run as a separate service
  - Ollama                  (MIT)
  - n8n                     (Sustainable Use License) — optional profile
  - FastAPI, SQLAlchemy,
    Pydantic, Uvicorn,
    httpx, psycopg          (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0)
  - Obsidian                (proprietary, free for personal use) — host app;
                             ILE only reads/writes plain Markdown in a vault.

See docs/12-Licensing-Guide.md for the full dependency license inventory and
the compatibility rationale (notably why Metabase's AGPL scope is limited to
the separately deployed analytics container and does not affect ILE's
Apache-2.0 licensing).
